Prevent stale transport work from blocking pods

A detached startup can retain a pod's lifecycle mutex indefinitely when
a separate backend command stops responding. A successful host probe
does not complete that command, so reconnecting clients can remain
queued forever.

Bound read-only backend queries, host probe queues, tunnel setup, and
lifecycle waiters. Report the active operation, phase, and age without
exposing command arguments. Cancel owned local process groups on control
deadlines, while leaving builds, hooks, transfers, arbitrary commands,
and uncertain lifecycle mutations under their original owner's lock.

Replace remote tunnel process killing with a progress lease so a delayed
cleanup command cannot kill a replacement tunnel. Keep heartbeats
independent of forwarded stream handling. Interrupt pod event requests
and owned proxy sessions on host invalidation or HTTP observer
cancellation. Preserve TCP half-closes for forwarded services and detect
silent event transports with a read deadline that heartbeats renew.

Exercise delayed control completion over disposable OpenSSH hosts,
repeated outages, multiple pods, successful subsequent entry, detached
startup, and stream liveness. Reuse the existing process fixtures for
bounded assertions and cancellation cleanup checks.
